      "is_best": true,
      "html": "<div class=\"post__content post__content--new-editor\"><p>Hello ​<user-mention data-id=\"36018\">@Wood.Andy</user-mention> </p><p>Starting from <strong>STM32CubeIDE 2.0.0,</strong> STM32CubeMX is no longer integrated as a plugin inside CubeIDE, so the two tools now work separately. </p><p>See <a href=\"https://community.st.com/t5/stm32cubeide-mcus/stm32cubeide-2-0-0-released/td-p/857110#:~:text=With%20this%20release%2C%20device%20configuration%2C%20previously%20handled%20within%C2%A0STM32CubeIDE%C2%A0via%C2%A0STM32CubeMX%2C%20is%20now%20exclusively%20available%20through%20the%20stand-alone%C2%A0STM32CubeMX%C2%A0tool.\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_self\"><em>STM32CubeIDE 2.0.0 released</em></a>.</p><p> <a href=\"https://community.st.com/t5/stm32-mcus/stm32cubeide-2-0-0-workflow-tutorial/ta-p/864831\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_self\"><em>STM32CubeIDE 2.0.0 New workflow tutorial</em></a></p><p>BR, Souhaib</p></div>"
    },
    {
      "is_best": false,
      "html": "<div class=\"post__content post__content--new-editor\"><p>Yes, I do know that, I have commented on it before - check the forum...</p><p>But you would not expect it to screw up the previous version - especially after all the comments on here about it...</p></div>"
